course: dictionary
lesson: 12941
title: Digging up the past
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An excavation is digging in the ground, done carefully, often to find old things. Archaeologists, the people who study the past, carry out excavations to find bones, pots and coins. «The team began an excavation near the old Roman wall.» Digging carefully is the key clue here.
explain: The word can mean three things. It can be the digging itself, a place where digging is happening, or digging a big hole for building. Read the words around it to see which one fits. «The builders started the excavation for the new car park on Monday.» Here it means digging a big hole for building.
explain: Try the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: «The team started the digging near the old Roman wall» still makes sense, so you have understood it. Notice the safety word in the rules: «Keep out of the excavation.» Excavations are deep holes, so they can be dangerous.
fact: «Excavation» means digging in the ground, especially carefully, to find old things.
fact: Archaeologists carry out excavations to find things such as bones, pots and coins.
fact: «Excavation» can also mean the place where the digging is done, which is called a dig.
fact: On building sites, «excavation» means digging a big hole, for example for a basement or tunnel.
fact: Excavations are deep holes, so keep out of them unless you are with a grown-up who is allowed to be there.
exercise: «The archaeologists spent a summer on an excavation, carefully brushing soil from an old pot.» What is an excavation? | A type of bird that lives by the sea | *Digging carefully in the ground to find old things | Painting a wall with a brush | A kind of cake baked in a tin
exercise: «The builders started the excavation for the new car park on Monday.» What is the excavation here? | *Digging a big hole for building | A bright light shining at night | Old bones in a museum | A picnic on the grass
exercise: The sign says «Excavation: keep out.» What does the sign tell you? | *Stay away, because it is a deep hole | Free ice cream for everyone | Come closer to see the bones | Bring a spade and join in
test: «Scientists made an excavation in the desert and found a small clay pot.» Find and copy one word that means digging carefully to find old things. | desert | *excavation | scientists | clay
test: In history lessons, what do archaeologists look for during an excavation? | Maps of the ocean floor | *Old things such as Roman coins or dinosaur bones | Sweets and crisps | New cars and bikes
exam: Ella says an excavation is a kind of party. Why is she wrong? | *An excavation is digging in the ground, often to find old things | An excavation is a bus that goes to the beach | An excavation is a party with cake and games | An excavation is a type of weather
